WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:12.405
 Reader beware--
you're in for a scare.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:21.770
My job is to scare people,
but in this master class,

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:25.945
I hope to teach you that writing
doesn't have to be scary.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.250
When you start to write,
do a complete outline.

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:35.830
I start generally
with the ending.

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:39.070
If I know the ending, then
I can spend the whole book

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:43.020
fooling the reader.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:45.990
I was a really fearful
kid, and I was always

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:49.020
sure something was
lurking in the garage.

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:52.380
Now, I can remember
that feeling of panic,

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:56.280
and I can bring it back and
try to put it into my books.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:58.590
If you're writing for
kids, think about the age

00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:00.060
of the audience constantly.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:03.330
My big rule for writing
middle-grade harder

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:07.900
is that they have to
know it's a fantasy.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.170
The real world can't interfere.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.870
There's no divorce.

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:12.900
No guns.

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:14.250
No one ever dies.

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:16.680
Once you've
established that, you

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:20.610
can go pretty far
with the scares.

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:23.740
Writing for teens is
kind of the opposite.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:26.410
It has to be very real.

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:28.608
They have to believe
this is happening.

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:34.250
I grew up in a very
wealthy suburb,

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:36.890
but my family was really poor.

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:39.350
I always felt like an outsider.

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:42.810
I was on the
sidelines observing,

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:44.470
and that's one
reason why I stayed

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:46.300
in my room writing so much.

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:48.250
That's the appeal
of writing anyway.

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:50.470
You're here creating
your own universe.

00:01:53.122 --> 00:01:55.250
In this master
class, we're going

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:57.620
to talk about how
to go about getting

00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:02.210
ideas, how I use twists, how
I come up with cliffhangers.

00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:06.556
And I'm going to tell you how
never to get writer's block.

00:02:06.556 --> 00:02:09.389
I will take you through
the whole process

00:02:09.389 --> 00:02:12.610
and show you that
none of this is scary.

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:17.370
I'm R. L. Stein, and
this is my master class.

